      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "CABG surgery has been considered the optimal revascularization strategy for patients with diabetes mellitus who have lexft main and/or multivessel coronary artery disease. The results of a new analysis of data from the SYNTAX trial challenge this conventional wisdom and highlight additional coronary revascularization options to physicians and patients."},
